  "releaseNotes": "Added AfasClient.UsingAuthentication to use a custom IAfasAuthentication strategy; the authentication constructor is now also available to subclasses. ClientCredentialsAuthentication considers a token expired 25% of its lifetime (at most 60 seconds) before it expires, so short-lived tokens are cached as well, and its exceptions contain only the HTTP status and the OAuth error code, never the response body. Corrected the classic token dates: existing classic tokens expire on 1 May 2027, and app connectors that use a classic token stop working after 31 August 2027.",
